```java
private BigDecimal parseResidual(String raw) {
    String value = raw.trim();
    if (!RESIDUAL_PATTERN.matcher(value).matches()) {
        throw ApiException.badRequest("residualAmount 必须为 0~100 毫克、最多 6 位小数的十进制字符串");
    }
    BigDecimal amount = new BigDecimal(value);
    if (amount.compareTo(MAX_SUBMITTABLE) > 0) {
        throw ApiException.badRequest("residualAmount 超出 0~100 毫克范围");
    }
    return amount;
}
```
Note: pattern `^(0|[1-9]\d{0,2})(\.\d{1,6})?$` — "100" matches [1-9]\d{0,2} → "100" ✓. "100.000001" → matches pattern (100 + .000001) but > 100 → 400 ✓. "0.100001" ✓. "00.5" rejected ✓. ".5" rejected — hmm, should ".5" be allowed? Spec: decimal string; rejecting is fine (strict). "5." rejected ✓.

